{"type":"npc","name":"Toyblox","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":65,"temp":0,"max":65,"details":""},"ac":{"value":22,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"critical-hits","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":"Can't speak any language"},"level":{"value":5},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Originating from the dreams of children, a toyblox appears to the untrained eye to be a mundane toy box that can mysteriously produce any toy. Toybloxes feed on proximity to children's imaginative thoughts. Most toybloxes form a bond with a specific child, whom they entertain, inspire, and protect from danger.</p><h2>No Time to Play</h2><p>As children develop more responsibilities and have less time for play, toybloxes do what they can to encourage them to retain their sense of wonder and imagination. Still, most toybloxes depart for new opportunities at some point in the child's teenage years, though those who look back fondly on their experiences might choose to entertain that child's younger relatives or even their future children.</p><p>Toyblox that remain bonded to a child for several years sometimes develops additional abilities to manipulate their surroundings to fit that child's desires. If not handled carefully, this growth can lead to towns becoming unstable playgrounds of oozing nonsense.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 18/45/80 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Crafting, Occultism, Society, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, dexterity, energy resistant (vitality), fortification, intelligence, mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), space, space shield, spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.HBJPsonQnWcC3qdX]{Mirage}), strength, throwing, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Gabriel Regli","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":5},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":1},"int":{"mod":5},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":1}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":12,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":8,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":12,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":11},"athletics":{"base":13},"crafting":{"base":13},"occultism":{"base":10},"society":{"base":12},"stealth":{"base":11}},"traits":{"value":["ooze"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"SgOQYk15XW8eDCaV","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/toyblox.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Toyblox","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/toyblox.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/toyblox.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"name":"Occult Innate Spells","type":"spellcastingEntry","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"ability":{"value":"cha"},"spelldc":{"value":14,"dc":22},"tradition":{"value":"occult"},"prepared":{"value":"innate"},"showSlotlessLevels":{"value":false},"proficiency":{"value":1},"slots":{"slot0":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot1":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot2":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot3":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot4":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot5":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot6":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot7":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot8":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot9":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot10":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot11":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0}},"autoHeightenLevel":{"value":null}},"_id":"8iSA2q2BOT0IJ5iz","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/spellcastingEntry.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"folder":"7cyoYPoPYA01mErU","img":"icons/environment/wilderness/cave-entrance-vulcano.webp","name":"Mirage","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You create an illusion that causes natural terrain to look, sound, feel, and smell like a different kind of terrain. This doesn't disguise any structures or creatures in the area.</p>\n<p>Any creature that touches the illusion or uses the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.BlAOM2X92SI6HMtJ]{Seek} action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (5th)</strong> Your image can also disguise structures or create illusory structures (but still doesn't disguise creatures).</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"mirage","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","illusion","manipulate"],"rarity":"uncommon","traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":4},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":"500 feet"},"area":{"type":"burst","value":50},"time":{"value":"10 minutes"},"duration":{"value":"until your next daily preparations","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"8iSA2q2BOT0IJ5iz"},"counteraction":false},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.HBJPsonQnWcC3qdX","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"nIyZH1WCgpkIr1Ab"},{"type":"action","name":"Plush Defense","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature targets the toyblox with an attack and the toyblox can see the attacker</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The toyblox manifests a plush toy between itself and the incoming blow, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[{"key":"RollOption","option":"plush-defense","toggleable":true},{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":"ac","value":2,"predicate":["plush-defense"],"type":"circumstance"}],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"o4j4wYXVgIEHtCc1","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Toy Chest","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>The toyblox has a hollow interior, which it can use to store up to 25 Bulk worth of items without being encumbered. It can release any number of objects held within by spending a manipulate action. It can also allow other creatures to take what it is holding. When the toyblox is within a creature's reach, a creature can Interact with the toyblox to stow or retrieve items as if it were a mundane box. If the toyblox is not willing to have the object stowed or retrieved, the creature must first succeed at a @Check[athletics|dc:25] check.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"vLngl0IK11iq8KKh","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Temporary Toy","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>1 minute. The toyblox conjures forth a temporary toy, which must have a total size of 1 cubic foot or smaller and lasts for 1 hour. The toy can include multiple pieces, such as a jigsaw puzzle, and it can include moving parts. The toy is sturdy enough to survive typical use, though it isn't usually suitable for use as an improvised weapon. It can take the form of a common level 0 piece of adventuring gear with a value of 1 gp or less, but it can't typically replicate more complex or expensive items.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","occult"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"esHrWhsjxeeELKUO","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Tidy Up","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p>The toyblox tidies up its environment. All unattended objects within 30 feet fly into the toyblox's internal toy chest. If the items would exceed the toy chest's bulk limit, the toyblox chooses which items to leave behind. Non-magical dust, dirt, and grime disappear from all objects and surfaces within the range. The toyblox attempts a counteract check (counteract modifier [[/r 1d20+12 #Counteract]]{+12}) against magical sources of mess in the area, such as the grease spell. If the counteract check fails, it can't attempt to Tidy Up that same effect a second time.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["manipulate","occult"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"ma8MOUmr79XkLump","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Put That Away!","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p>The toyblox last action was a successful slamming lid Strike against a creature of size Large or smaller</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The toyblox disapproves of the use of dangerous objects like weapons. The toyblox attempts to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Dt6B1slsBy8ipJu9]{Disarm} the creature, ignoring the typical requirement of having a free hand. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the toyblox's multiple attack penalty.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.4.1"}},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"bk3TcFLIDB2kXB3N","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Conjure Guardian","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p>The toyblox conjures a giant toy soldier, which uses the statistics of animated armor. It can Sustain the toy soldier for up to 1 minute. The soldier is metaphysically linked to the toyblox's life force. If the toy soldier is reduced to 0 Hit Points, the toyblox takes @Damage[10[untyped]] damage.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","lice